{
  "name": "Nayancode Workbench",
  "biotoolsID": "nayancode",
  "version": [
    "1.1.0"
  ],
  "description": "Free, open-source bioinformatics and cheminformatics in the web browser. Twenty-seven studios: Docking (AutoDock Vina 1.2.7 in WebAssembly, receptor and ligand preparation, virtual screens); Genome (FASTQ QC, minimap2 mapping, samtools, bcftools SNV and indel calling, genome viewer, bundled genomes, CRISPR off-targets); Variant (VCF filtering, signatures, ClinVar/gnomAD/VEP evidence); Expression (RNA-seq differential expression for any design, enrichment); Single-Cell (clustering, UMAP); Microbiome (diversity, UniFrac, PERMANOVA); Chemistry (RDKit descriptors, QSAR); Structure (Mol* viewer, interactions); Phylogenetics (alignment, maximum-likelihood trees); Sequence (primers, cloning, restriction digests, CRISPR guides); Lab (qPCR, IC50, power); CRISPR (guide design, off-targets); Primer (design, in-silico PCR, dimers); Enrichment (ORA, GSEA); Protocol (master mix, timers, notebook); Sanger (ABIF viewer, trimming, comparison); Image Counter (colony counting, watershed); Flow (FCS import, compensation, gating, statistics). Files stay on the user's computer; every result records provenance and methods text.",
  "homepage": "https://solagene.com/nayancode/",
